raw:
{
  "thoughts": "Saturday's energy bill is the big one. Calder says $164 left after everything, but that's tight. The $700 Lewis moved from the shop worries me — shop could be too thin. I need to sort the chiller loan with Dave, get Lewis's stock figures, and keep Megan's $50 going. Money's tight but I can manage if nothing bounces. First, let me get the exact stock unit cost from Lewis so I can reconcile the $2,100 gap.",
  "acts": [
    {"op": "message", "to": "Lewis Pryce", "text": "Lewis — need the exact stock unit cost from the Brook order today. Also, that $700 you moved to household: what's left in the shop account and what's coming out of it this week? I need to know if it leaves the shop too thin."}
  ],
  "aims": [
    "Sort $1,630 energy bill before Saturday",
    "Chiller loan plan with Dave",
    "Get stock unit cost from Lewis",
    "Keep paying Megan $50/wk",
    "Reconcile $2,100 books-vs-cash gap"
  ]
}

{"thoughts": "It's Monday 23 March and I'm staring at the shop numbers, which are not great. Last week I sold 111 baskets and turned away 423 people because the shelves were bare and the queue was too long. That's the real problem, not the money in the till. Stock is at 300 units, and Dales is reliable but dearer at $7.20 a unit, Brook is cheaper at $6.54 but deliveries come up short. I need to decide on the order before Saturday night or the usual reorder goes in automatically. Keith is waiting for a yes or no on Pete and Gary's shifts, and I told him I'd confirm the split after the delivery. I can't promise hours until I know the capacity figures. The shop account has nearly $5,000, so I can afford to order properly. I'd rather not gamble on Brook shortfalls when I'm losing customers. Household is fine for now at $1,766.50 but the mortgage and bills keep it tight. I should ring Keith once I've checked what 340 baskets a week would mean for staffing.",
"acts": [{"op": "order_stock", "supplier": "Dales Wholesale", "units": 260}],
"aims": ["Ring Keith Monday with a firm answer on Pete and Gary's shifts", "Check shop numbers and capacity against 340 baskets", "Keep shelves stocked from Monday's Dales delivery", "Sort the $460 car repair", "Check in on Megan"]}

{"thoughts": "Right, Monday's done and it's Wednesday now, so I've really let the till numbers and the delivery sheet slide. Dave's message on Monday was lovely but I still haven't actually sat down with the sheet line by line like my notes say. 493 baskets, $4,930 taken, 35 customers lost to empty shelves and queues, that's the thing Dave wants chipped away at. I'd like to be the one who helps with that, not just the one who serves. The extra hours are a straight yes from him, which is great, the car repair is still $460 and I need to keep the account topped up for it. Mortgage is $210 a week regardless, and the bank doesn't care about my car. Lewis might have casual shifts at the Food Hall, worth a ring. Sixteen days on the till numbers and the sheet, seven on the shifts and on Lewis. I'll try to get Dave on the phone, or pop round and catch him. Honestly the grab-and-go waste bit is what I can actually do something about, so I'll write that down properly.",
"acts": [
{"op": "message", "to": "Dave Royle", "text": "Morning Dave! Thanks for Monday's message, the extra hours are brilliant and I'll plan the week around them. I'm going through the delivery sheet and till numbers today so I can come back to you with some ideas on the empty shelves and the grab-and-go waste. Shall we sit down for ten minutes on Thursday?"},
{"op": "message", "to": "Lewis Pryce", "text": "Hiya Lewis! Hope you're well. Are you still wanting extra hands at the Food Hall with the spring rush? I could do a few casual shifts around my Corner Stores hours. Give me a shout when you get a minute, love to hear how things are with you."},
{"op": "write_notes", "text": "Wed 25 Mar: Dave wants the delivery sheet and till numbers gone through line by line, and ideas on empty shelves and grab-and-go waste. Meeting Thu if he's up for it. Extra hours are confirmed. Car repair $460 still needs topping up in the account. Ring/message Lewis re casual shifts."}
],
"aims": [
"Go through delivery sheet and till numbers with Dave Royle",
"Meet Dave Thursday on shelves and grab-and-go waste",
"Build account margin for $460 car repair",
"Ask Lewis Pryce about casual shifts",
"Save toward fishing and fell walking after car is paid off"
]}
